{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_019ZJHBJNSdFJw3NRrAftjVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**Q8: Walk through a production-ready agent architecture** → `answers/03-008-walk-through-a-production-ready-agent-architecture.md`\n\nThe answer covers a **six-layer architecture**:\n\n1. **Interface/Session** — FastAPI + Redis session store (TTL 30 min)\n2. **Loop controller** — `max_iterations=15`, `wall_clock_timeout=120s`, per-step token budget; termination via goal signal, budget exhaustion, or HITL\n3. **Tiered LLM** — GPT-4o-mini for tool dispatch/routing (cheap), GPT-4o for planning/synthesis; T=0 for deterministic tool calls\n4. **Tool execution** — strict JSON schemas (cuts hallucinated args 40–60%), pre-call PII scrub via Presidio, sandboxed execution (E2B/Docker), idempotency keys + 3-retry exponential backoff\n5. **Four-tier memory** — working (context window), episodic (Redis), semantic (Pinecone/Qdrant), procedural (system prompt)\n6. **Observability + Safety** — LangSmith step traces, LangGraph `interrupt_before` HITL for irreversible actions, NeMo Guardrails, Redis checkpointing for crash recovery\n\nKey pitfalls called out: no budget caps, GPT-4o for every step, treating memory as just the context window."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":66437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5abab83-3367-4fbb-9db2-71cda27e0b81","uuid":"895f439a-18a7-4a82-a3e0-134683b2336b"}
